	"title" "意图乱流 Intent Chaos"
	"description" "[h1]Intent Chaos 意图乱流[/h1]\nMonster intents are no longer fixed loops — when a monster takes real HP damage from your direct attacks, it immediately rerolls its intent to a random different move from its entire move pool.\n\n[h2]Core Mechanics[/h2]\n[list]\n[*]A monster that loses HP to a [b]direct attack[/b] instantly rerolls its intent, and it is guaranteed to land on a different move\n[*]Passive damage from relics, potions, powers and end-of-turn effects does [b]not[/b] trigger rerolls\n[*]No trigger on fully blocked hits (no HP lost) or on kills\n[*]Random picks use the game's synchronized multiplayer RNG, so both clients stay in sync\n[/list]\n\n[h2]Boss Rules[/h2]\n[list]\n[*]All bosses reroll from their very first move\n[*][b]The Queen (Act 3) exception: her first three moves stay fixed[/b], then she joins the random pool\n[*]Every boss gains one extra move in its pool: [b]Curse Card[/b] — when rolled, it [b]permanently[/b] adds a curse card to your deck, and instantly shuffles a copy into your current draw pile\n[*]That move shows the purple summon icon on top of the monster's head; hover over it for details\n[/list]\n\n[h2]Scripted Moves Stay Put (v0.3.0 / v0.3.1)[/h2]\n[list]\n[*][b]Death blow and self-destruct moves are never touched.[/b] The Waterfall Giant survives its first death, its HP bar turns infinite, and only its own explosion can end the fight — that intent is pinned, so the boss always dies properly\n[*]Same for moves the game itself locks (must-perform recharge and revive states) and for moves that show no icon at all: a Decimillipede limb's blank reattach-chain move can no longer land on a healthy limb, so you never get an intent that does nothing and never changes\n[*]Escape, sleep and stun moves stay out of the random pool [b]and[/b] are never rerolled away — a one-way blacklist used to delete a move for the rest of the fight\n[*]Stuck saves self-repair: if a boss is sitting at infinite HP without its death blow, the mod puts the self-destruct move back the next time it takes damage\n[/list]\n\n[h2]Compatibility[/h2]\n[list]\n[*]Pure code mod with zero dependencies — coexists with character mods, BaseLib, etc.\n[*]Self-adapts to game versions at runtime (minor updates need no maintenance; on a major rewrite the mod puts itself to sleep to protect your game — never crashes it)\n[*]Verified from 0.107.1 through 0.111.0, stable and beta\n[/list]\n\n\n\n[h1]意图乱流 Intent Chaos[/h1]\n怪物的意图不再是固定循环——受到你的直接攻击并真实掉血后，它会立刻从自己的全部招式池里随机换一个别的意图。\n\n[h2]核心机制[/h2]\n[list]\n[*]怪物被[b]直接攻击[/b]造成[b]真实掉血[/b] → 该怪物意图立刻重掷，且保证换成不同的招式\n[*]遗物、药水、能力牌、回合结束等[b]被动伤害不触发[/b]\n[*]被格挡完全挡下（不掉血）、怪物死亡：不触发\n[*]怪物随机选招使用联机同步 RNG，多人游戏下两端一致\n[/list]\n\n[h2]BOSS 规则[/h2]\n[list]\n[*]所有 boss 从第一招起就参与随机\n[*][b]女王（第三层）特例：开场三招固定不变[/b]，之后才参与随机\n[*]boss 招式池额外含一招 [b]【塞诅咒牌】[/b]：被随机到时会[b]永久[/b]往你的卡组加一张诅咒牌——战斗结束也不会移除，同时立刻塞一张进本战抽牌堆\n[*]该招式头顶显示紫色召唤物图样，鼠标悬停可查看说明\n[/list]\n\n[h2]脚本类招式保持固定（v0.3.0 / v0.3.1）[/h2]\n[list]\n[*][b]亡语、自爆类招式绝不被改动。[/b]瀑布巨兽第一次死透后会进入血条无限的约爆状态，只能靠自己自爆才能结束战斗——这个意图被钉住了，所以它一定能正常退场\n[*]本体自己锁定的招式（必须执行一次的蓄力、重生类），以及“头顶什么都不显示”的占位招，同样不动：千足虫断肢的空白意图不会再落到活肢体身上，你也就不会再遇到一个“什么都不做、再打也不变”的意图\n[*]逃跑、睡眠、眩晕类招式既不进随机池，也不会被从当前招换走——以前那是单向门，换走就再也回不来，等于把这招从怪身上删掉\n[*]已经卡死的存档会自动救场：不死的 boss 下次受伤时，自爆招被放回去\n[/list]\n\n[h2]兼容性[/h2]\n[list]\n[*]纯代码 mod，无前置依赖，与角色 mod、BaseLib 等共存\n[*]运行时自适应游戏版本（小版本更新免维护；大改版会自动休眠保护游戏，不会崩溃）\n[*]已在 0.107.1 至 0.111.0 验证，稳定版与测试版通用\n[/list]"
	"changenote" "v0.3.1 结构性招式双向固定（在 v0.3.0 亡语/自爆之外）：再固定两类本体脚本招——空白意图招（零意图或意图全为 HiddenIntent，例如千足虫断肢重生链的链头 DEAD_MOVE）与必须执行一次的锁定招（千足虫 REATTACH、实验体 RESPAWN）。它们既不会被随机发到别的怪身上（此前活肢体会顶着一个什么都不做、再打也不变的空意图），也不会被从当前招换走（换走会打断重生脚本；锁定招连本体自己都换不走，意图会钉死）。想保留更多花样可在 config 里关 pinStructuralMoves。Scripted blank-intent and must-perform revive moves are now pinned both ways: split limbs no longer sit on a do-nothing blank intent."
}
